# The two variables the site needs, and the only two. Copy to `.env.local` for
# local development; set both in the Vercel project for a deployment.
#
# Nothing secret belongs here. Vite inlines every `VITE_`-prefixed variable into
# the client bundle, so anything in this file ships to every visitor. That is
# fine for both of these - a contract address is public by construction, and the
# site never holds a key, because every view it calls is read-only and unsigned.

# The deployed ReputationOracle. Changes on every redeploy; a build without it
# renders as "unconfigured" rather than failing, so an empty value here is a
# legitimate state and not an error.
#
# This is the address the README documents as the live studionet deployment. It
# previously drifted a redeploy behind the README, which reads as an empty
# registry rather than as a misconfiguration - so the two are kept in step
# deliberately, and both have to move together on the next deploy.
VITE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=0x1903b01a14053c2322ede4373669F411Dcd2Cd05

# Which network to read that address from, by the alias the GenLayer CLI uses:
# localnet | studionet | testnet-asimov | testnet-bradbury
#
# Must match the network the address above was deployed to. It is not checked
# against the chain, and a mismatch reads an address that does not exist there,
# which surfaces as an empty registry rather than as a misconfiguration.
# Defaults to studionet when unset; an unrecognised value throws at startup.
#
# Studionet is where this contract is deployed, and it is *not* a network where
# payouts arrive: a contract cannot pay an externally owned account there, so
# every release, claim, refund and bond reclaim is recorded correctly over money
# that never moves. The site says so where it offers those actions.
#
# To settle for real, point this at `testnet-asimov` or `testnet-bradbury` and
# deploy there - the contract and the client need no change for it. See the
# README's "Settlement" section, and `npm run settlement`, which confirms the
# studionet limitation and verifies the payouts anywhere they can complete.
VITE_GENLAYER_NETWORK=studionet
